lass=3D"md-content__inner md-typeset"> <h1 id=3D"optimise-a-cbot-in-ctrader=
">Optimise a cBot in cTrader</h1> <p>This article explains <a href=3D"https=
://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/how-tos/cbots/optimize-a-cbot/"><strong>ho=
w to optimise trading bots</strong></a> in cTrader Windows and Mac. </p> <p=
>It can be difficult to specify an optimal set of initial parameters for a =
cBot. Luckily, cTrader offers a built-in cBot optimisation feature. Optimis=
ation takes your code and runs it several times with each pass being based =
on various parameter values. It then presents you with a set of customisabl=
e results which you can use to define the optimal parameter configuration.<=
/p> <p>To use this feature, select a cBot instance and switch to the <stron=
g>Optimisation</strong> tab.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image title" src=
=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/img/updated/backtesting-optimizat=
ion.png"></p> </figure> <p>Afterwards, define the backtesting period for op=
timisation by using the dropdown calendars or by dragging the slider.</p> <=
figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image title" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader=
-algo/img/updated/backtesting-opt-slider.png"></p> </figure> <h2 id=3D"opti=
misation-settings">Optimisation settings</h2> <p>As optimisation is essenti=
ally just a series of backtests, you can specify backtesting settings simil=
arly to how it is done in the <a href=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-a=
lgo/documentation/cbots/backtest-a-cbot/"><strong>Backtesting tab</strong><=
/a>.</p> <h2 id=3D"optimisation-parameters">Optimisation parameters</h2> <p=
>Click the <strong>Parameters</strong> button to the left of the calendar s=
lider. You should see the following window.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Ima=
ge title" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/img/updated/optimiza=
tion-parameters.png"></p> </figure> <p>In it, check the flags next to the c=
Bot parameters that you would like to optimise. The <strong>Timeframe</stro=
ng> parameter is available for all cBots.</p> <h2 id=3D"optimisation-criter=
ia">Optimisation criteria</h2> <p>Press the <strong>Criteria</strong> butto=
n located to the right of the <strong>Optimisation parameters</strong> butt=
on. cTrader will open the following tab.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image =
title" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/img/updated/backtesting=
-opt-criteria.png"></p> </figure> <p>Optimisation criteria define how the o=
ptimisation algorithm ranks your result after backtesting. You can choose b=
etween the following options:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Standard</strong> - a se=
ries of predefined criteria that you can aim to either minimise or maximise=
. To do this, choose a criterion from a dropdown menu to the right and sele=
ct the optimisation direction in its related menu to the left. To add a new=
 criterion, click <strong>Add criterion</strong>.</li> <li><strong>Custom</=
strong> - a custom criterion defined within your cBot code using the <code =
class=3D"highlight"><span class=3D"n">GetFitness</span><span class=3D"p">()=
</span></code> method as shown in the below examples.</li> </ul> <div class=
