</code></pre></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div> </div> </div> </div> <h=
3 id=3D"multi-criteria-calculations">Multi-criteria calculations</h3> <p>If=
 multiple criteria are used to calculate parameter effectiveness, cTrader w=
ill use all of them equally to calculate the fitness value for an optimisat=
ion pass.</p> <p>Specifically, the platform multiplies the values of all ma=
ximising criteria and separately multiplies the values of all minimising cr=
iteria. Subsequently, it divides the absolute multiplication value for the =
maximising criteria by the same value for the minimising criteria.</p> <p>T=
he following pseudocode shows exactly how multi-criteria fitness values are=
 calculated.</p> <div class=3D"highlight"><table class=3D"highlighttable"><=
tbody><tr><td class=3D"linenos"><div class=3D"linenodiv"><pre><span></span>=
<span class=3D"normal"> 1</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 2</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 3</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 4</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 5</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 6</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 7</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 8</span>
<span class=3D"normal"> 9</span>
<span class=3D"normal">10</span>
<span class=3D"normal">11</span>
<span class=3D"normal">12</span>
<span class=3D"normal">13</span></pre></div></td><td class=3D"code"><div><p=
re id=3D"__code_5"><span></span><nav class=3D"md-code__nav"><button class=
=3D"md-code__button" title=3D"Copy to clipboard" data-clipboard-target=3D"#=
__code_5 &gt; code" data-md-type=3D"copy"></button></nav><code>numerator =
=3D 1.0
if (valuesToMaximize.Length &gt; 0)
    numerator =3D Abs(Multiply(criteriaValuesToMaximize))

denominator =3D 1.0
if (valuesToMinimize.Length &gt; 0)
    denominator +=3D Abs(Multiply(criteriaValuesToMinimize))

/* The 'sign' variable can be either +` or -1 depending on whether
there are criteria for which their values are less than 0. */
sign =3D criteriaValuesToMinimize.Concat(criteriaValuesToMaximize).Any(v =
=3D&gt; v &lt; 0) ? -1 : 1

fitness =3D  sign * numerator / denominator
</code></pre></div></td></tr></tbody></table></div> <h2 id=3D"method">Metho=
d</h2> <p>Click the <strong>Method</strong> button (represented either as <=
code>GA</code> or <code>#</code> depending on which option is chosen). In t=
he below menu, choose which optimisation method is used by the platform.</p=
> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image title" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctra=
der-algo/img/updated/backtesting-opt-algorithm.png"></p> </figure> <p>The f=
ollowing options are available:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Genetic Algorithm</str=
ong> - the algorithm emulates the biological evolution process. Please <a h=
ref=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/guides/optimization/genetic-al=
gorithm/"><strong>see a separate section</strong></a> for its detailed desc=
ription.</li> <li><strong>Grid (#)</strong> - the algorithm sequentially ba=
cktests each possible set of parameters.</li> </ul> <div class=3D"admonitio=
n note"> <p class=3D"admonition-title">Note</p> <p>In our estimation, the g=
enetic algorithm is significantly faster for finding optimal parameter valu=
es.</p> </div> <h2 id=3D"resources">Resources</h2> <p>Click the <strong>Res=
ources</strong> button to select which percentage of your CPU load is alloc=
ated for backtesting. Move the slider to set the CPU usage percentage.</p> =
<p>The more resources you allocate, the faster the optimisation process wil=
l be completed. However, you may see a drop in performance when using other=
 applications.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image title" src=3D"https://help=
.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/img/updated/backtest-opt-resources.png"></p> </fi=
gure> <p>Note that the CPU resources can also be adjusted during optimisati=
on itself.</p> <h2 id=3D"start-and-manage-the-optimisation-procedure">Start=
 and manage the optimisation procedure</h2> <p>To proceed with optimisation=
, click the <strong>Play</strong> button to the right of the calendar slide=
r. Depending on your machine resources, the optimisation settings, and cBot=
 complexity, optimisation may take some time.</p> <p>The UI bar immediately=
 below the calendar slider will provide information about the number of bac=
ktesting passes completed, the elapsed time and the remaining time estimate=
.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image title" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/=
ctrader-algo/img/updated/backtest-opt-passes.png"></p> </figure> <p>The cen=
tral screen in the <strong>Optimisation</strong> tab, meanwhile, will provi=
de a real-time grid containing information about all of the backtesting pas=
ses that the algorithm has completed.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=3D"Image tit=
le" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/img/updated/optimization-p=
asses-new.png"></p> </figure> <p>To apply a set of parameters tested during=
 a certain pass, click the <strong>Apply</strong> button. It only becomes a=
ctive if no optimisation procedures are currently running.</p> <p>Alternati=
vely, check the <strong>Autoselect the best pass</strong> flag in the upper=
-left corner for cTrader to automatically select the pass (and the paramete=
rs) that has achieved the best possible result according to your specified =
optimisation criteria.</p> <h2 id=3D"optimisation-results">Optimisation res=
ults</h2> <p>After optimisation is complete, the central table will display=
 the final list of all backtesting passes and their results.</p> <p>This ta=
ble has the following columns. As the grid is fully configurable, these col=
umns can be dragged-and-dropped or disabled altogether after right-clicking=
 the table and deselecting them from the contextual menu.</p> <div class=3D=
"md-typeset__scrollwrap"><div class=3D"md-typeset__table"><table> <thead> <=
tr> <th style=3D"text-align: center;">Field</th> <th>Definition</th> </tr> =
</thead> <tbody> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center;">Pass</td> <td>The p=
ass number.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center;">Fitness</td> =
<td>The value showcasing how well the pass fits the optimisation criteria.<=
/td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center;">Equity</td> <td>Total equ=
ity at the end of the pass.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center=
;">Balance</td> <td>Total balance at the end of the pass.</td> </tr> <tr> <=
td style=3D"text-align: center;">Net profit</td> <td>The difference between=
 the final balance and the starting balance.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"t=
ext-align: center;">Trades</td> <td>The total number of closed positions.</=
td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center;">Winning trades</td> <td>Th=
e total number of winning trades achieved during the pass.</td> </tr> <tr> =
<td style=3D"text-align: center;">Losing trades</td> <td>The total number o=
f losing trades achieved during the pass.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text=
-align: center;">Profit factor</td> <td>The total profit/total loss ratio.<=
/td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center;">*Max equity drawdown (%)<=
/td> <td>The maximum percentage of the equity drawdown.</td> </tr> <tr> <td=
 style=3D"text-align: center;">Max balance drawdown (%)</td> <td>The maximu=
m percentage of the balance drawdown.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-ali=
gn: center;">Max equity drawdown</td> <td>The maximum equity drawdown speci=
fied in the account deposit currency.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-ali=
gn: center;">Max balance drawdown</td> <td>The maximum balance drawdown spe=
cified in the account deposit currency.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-a=
lign: center;">Average trade</td> <td>The average profit for all trades mad=
e during the pass.</td> </tr> <tr> <td style=3D"text-align: center;">Pass p=
arameters</td> <td>Click the <strong>Apply</strong> button in this column t=
o apply the parameters from this pass to your cBot.</td> </tr> </tbody> </t=
able></div></div> <p>Select a pass to view detailed statistics about it in =
the display below the central grid.</p> <p>The first seven tabs in this dis=
play provide the same information as <a href=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ct=
rader-algo/documentation/cbots/backtest-a-cbot/#backtesting-results"><stron=
g>the same tabs</strong></a> in the <strong>Backtesting</strong> window. Th=
e <strong>Pass parameters</strong> tab is unique to optimisation. </p> <h3 =
id=3D"pass-parameters">Pass parameters</h3> <p>The <strong>Pass parameters<=
/strong> tab provides the following information.</p> <figure> <p><img alt=
=3D"Image title" src=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/img/updated/b=
acktesting-opt-passparams.png"></p> </figure> <p>cTrader will highlight all=
 optimised parameters in green while any fixed parameters (not enabled in t=
he <a href=3D"https://help.ctrader.com/ctrader-algo/documentation/cbots/opt=
imise-a-cbot/#optimisation-parameters"><strong>Parameters menu</strong></a>=
) will remain unhighlighted.</p> <h2 id=3D"saving-and-loading-optimisation-=
results">Saving and loading optimisation results</h2> <p>cTrader also allow=
s for saving and loading optimisation results to and from a locally stored =
<code>.optres</code> file.</p> <div class=3D"admonition note"> <p class=3D"=
admonition-title">Note</p> <p>A <code>.optres</code> file is simply a colle=
ction of key-value pairs with keys representing various optimisation settin=
gs and metrics.</p> </div> <div class=3D"admonition tip"> <p class=3D"admon=
ition-title">Tip</p> <p>You can use <code>.optres</code> files to continue =
refining your cBots across multiple local machines without losing any progr=
ess. You can also feed data from this file to generative AI tools to try an=
d detect any patterns in the passes that your cBot has completed.</p> </div=
> <p>To save optimisation results, wait until the process is concluded and =
click the <strong>Save</strong> icon. In the file explorer dialogue, type t=
he file name and save the file.</p> <p>To load optimisation results, click =
the <strong>Load</strong> icon and select the required file in the file exp=
lorer window.</p> <figure> <p><a href=3D"https://ctrader.com/start-selling?=
